_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.031503306880863384,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":47.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.29400998,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Columbia Financial, Inc. operates as a bank holding company for Columbia Bank that provides banking and other financial services to businesses and consumers in the United States. The company offers deposit products, including non-interest and interest-bearing demand accounts, savings and club deposits, money market accounts, and certificates of deposit. It also provides commercial loans, including multifamily and commercial real estate, commercial business, and construction loans; residential loans, such as one-to-four family residential real estate and one-to-four family residential loans; consumer loans, which includes home equity loans and advances, as well as automobile, personal, unsecured, and overdraft lines of credit; and securities activities. In addition, the company offers title insurance products; wealth management services; and cash management services comprising remote deposit, lockbox service, sweep accounts, and escrow services. Columbia Financial, Inc. was founded in 1926 and is based in Fair Lawn, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas J. Kemly | President, CEO & Director | Age 67 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 749 people. Revenue per employee of $345K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $78K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Columbia Financial, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.0B market cap on $259M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","The business throws off $59M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.32\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 56.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss.","Shareholder yield of 2.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 29% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Analyzing Columbia Financial (CLBK) and Its Peers","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/analyzing-columbia-financial-clbk-and-its-peers.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794594771.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (CLBK) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/89/Price-Driven_Insight_from_CLBK_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111026114602_1794329162.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794329162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Investors Are Reacting To Columbia Financial (CLBK) Lower Profit And Dividend Affirmed","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-clbk/columbia-financial/news/how-investors-are-reacting-to-columbia-financial-clbk-lower","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794022268.579,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.92,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Is Columbia Financial (CLBK) Fully Priced Following Q3 Earnings And Higher Charge Offs?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-clbk/columbia-financial/news/is-columbia-financial-clbk-fully-priced-following-q3-earning","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793820157.899,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Columbia Financial (NASDAQ:CLBK) and Banco Comercial Portugues (OTCMKTS:BPCGY) Financial Survey","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/columbia-financial-nasdaqclbk-and-banco-comercial-portugues-otcmktsbpcg